I think you're encountering one of the biggest limitations of current AI coding agents: **they are considerably better at producing frontend code than at producing excellent frontend experiences.**

An agent can generate thousands of lines of React, implement a Three.js scene, install GSAP, and create dozens of components. Yet the result can still look mediocre, animations can feel disconnected, and half the interactions may not work.

And increasing the model's thinking level doesn't necessarily fix that.

My recommendation is to stop treating Gemini as a website designer that also writes code. Instead, build a workflow in which different tools handle art direction, implementation, animation, and visual verification.

There are some particularly useful tools and techniques for this.

